@page
@model PantheonModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "The Pantheon";
}

<section class="section section-dark">
    <div class="section-inner section-narrow">
        <p class="section-label">Six Gods, Six Schools</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">The Pantheon</h2>
        <div class="ornament-divider" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="200" height="30"><use href="#divider-ornament" /></svg></div>
        <p>
            Every spell a Hollow-touched soul learns traces back to one of six gods. To study a
            school of magic is to petition a god, whether the caster admits it or not. There is
            said to be a seventh, but no shrine has ever borne his mark, and no priest has ever
            spoken his name.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-dark">
    <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="feature-grid">
            <div class="feature-card reveal-up">
                <svg class="feature-icon" width="40" height="40" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#ankh-icon" /></svg>
                <h3>Saelia, the Calm</h3>
                <p>Goddess of healing and calm nature. Her symbol is the ankh, and her favor mends what war and ruin break.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card reveal-up">
                <svg class="feature-icon" width="40" height="40" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#lightning-icon" /></svg>
                <h3>Vorreth, the Storm</h3>
                <p>God of wild chaos and disaster. His symbol is the lightning bolt, called upon by those who court ruin on purpose.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card reveal-up">
                <svg class="feature-icon" width="40" height="40" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#skull-icon" /></svg>
                <h3>Morvane, the Vile</h3>
                <p>God of evil and necromancy. His symbol is the skull, and his following keeps to the dark corners of every town.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card reveal-up">
                <svg class="feature-icon" width="40" height="40" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#crossed-swords-icon" /></svg>
                <h3>Kaldrun, the Fist</h3>
                <p>God of war, weaponcraft, and strategy. His symbol is crossed weapons, honored by soldiers before every campaign.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card reveal-up">
                <svg class="feature-icon" width="40" height="40" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#eye-icon" /></svg>
                <h3>Ryneth, the Fool</h3>
                <p>God of trickery and illusion. His symbol is the eye, and old rumor claims he has long gone silent. No one can confirm it.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card reveal-up">
                <svg class="feature-icon" width="40" height="40" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#note-icon" /></svg>
                <h3>Senneva, the Song</h3>
                <p>Goddess of arts, love, and beauty. Her symbol is the note, and some say no temple to her still stands.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-dark">
    <div class="section-inner section-narrow">
        <p class="section-label">A Warning to Scholars</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">The Unnamed One</h2>
        <div class="ornament-divider" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="200" height="30"><use href="#divider-ornament" /></svg></div>
        <p>
            The six gods can enter the Hollow, and so, it seems, can the Hollow-touched; ordinary
            mortals cannot. This is how the gods know a Hollow-touched soul when they meet one.
            Above or behind all six, legend holds, stands a seventh, unnamed, said to grant the
            other gods their reach into the Hollow-touched, yet forbidden from ever commanding one
            directly. Nothing is confirmed. Draw your own conclusions.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>
